  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Taiwanese Hokkien folk song of the Hengchun peninsula in southern Pingtung, sung to a small set of named tunes such as Sixiangqi and Pingpudiao, with the singer accompanying himself on the long-necked two-string moon lute (the yueqin card stands in). The tradition reached national attention through the 1967 folk-song collecting campaign of Hsu Tsang-houei and Shih Wei-liang.",
